51af0045 (868 1793311336672 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f375") (src . "test: two timing rows wait for the event, not a clock\n\nTwo rows read red on a slower machine and green alone.\n\nchange-stream-client CLIENT-12 stops a subscriber, floods the daemon\nuntil its queue overflows, continues the subscriber and wants the\nlagging terminal. The flood is about 185 publications, one thin-client\ninsert each, since a batch is one publication and one frame: 60 to 70 s\nhere, past the subscriber's 120 s alarm on a slower machine, which\nkilled the client before it could read. This row's subscriber now has a\n900 s backstop (subscribe-bg-alarm!; every other caller keeps 120 s);\nthe row's own wait after the continue is unchanged. The pids it holds\nare killed on that wait's timeout before its output is read, and on a\nraise after the stop, and a timeout with no complete line is a red row,\nnot a raise.\n\neval-lang L20 asserted that the answer came in under 3 s. Most of that\ntime is core.sc starting from source, about 1.5 s here. What the row\nmeans is that the runner did not wait for its background child, so it\nnow asserts that the child's marker is not there at the answer, read\nbefore the four-second wait that shows the child never ran on. The\nanswer's time is in the row's text as a reading.\n\n- Tests: change-stream-client, eval-lang; rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 528))))
