dfc94a66 (1003 1793343243360 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f351") (src . "daemon: blocking file I/O yields to the scheduler, and a probe defers while a publication is in progress\n\nLong writes and folds in the store process blocked the whole VM, so a\ntimer or a connection-local read waited for the entire export or\ncommit. ffi.sc gains io-yield!, a cooperative yield reached through the\nactor-key seam sched.sc already installs: a true no-op outside a\nscheduler, when interrupts are disabled, while a stage-scoped fault is\narmed, or within 50 ms of the actor's last yield (monotonic clock). It\nsaves and rebinds theourgia-stage around the sleep and never unwinds.\natomic-write!, fsync! and fsync-dir! yield once at their end, and\nprogress! is the second yield point; a no-yield extent covers nested\ncalls. The lock service's calls do not yield, and the lock budget is\nunchanged.\n\nThe yields open a window in which the disk differs from the published\nsnapshot by the daemon's own work. store-loop wraps the handling of\nevery message in busy!, which sets publication-pending with\ndynamic-wind; probe-for-outside-change! reads the flag at its\nreload-send decision and, when set, computes its notes as today, sends\nno reload and traces reload-deferred. A hold stage\ncommit-before-publish sits in the write path right before the publish\nhook, beside the existing reload-before-publish.\n\nTests: test/io-yield.sc (the ticker's maximum gap during an export, a\nconnection-local read during the write loop, the no-op cases) and\ntest/publication-pending.sc (a probe during a held commit and a held\nreload defers, the flag is clear after every exit). change-stream.sc\nFRAME-09 and the slow-reload construction take an outside touch of the\nwriters directory as their generator instead of a probe inside a fold;\nthe latter also arms reload-before-publish and asserts the three-part\nframe order. rows-baseline follows the fixtures' new bytes.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 536))))
